<center><B>Displaying the last ten guestbook entries...</B></center>
<br>
<TABLE cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 width="100%">

<TR bgcolor=#333333><TD valign=top>Posted by <B>Dammiana</B> on <B>Saturday 10th March 2001 - 7:20:49 am</B></td><tr><td>Just a quick hello to our new members :) Welcome to our family and I look forward to getting to know you all better. May Tunare bless our paths together.</TD></TR><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><TR bgcolor=#333333><TD valign=top>Posted by <B>Joneod</B> on <B>Saturday 27th January 2001 - 1:58:01 pm</B></td><tr><td>Wasn't sure where you wanted comments about the new site.  Personally I think I like the new one better.  Seems easier to get around now.  No matter what though, keep up the GREAT work here.</TD></TR><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><TR bgcolor=#333333><TD valign=top>Posted by <B>Shaddup Andcolor</B> on <B>Thursday 18th January 2001 - 2:00:01 pm</B></td><tr><td>Well I have looked at this site a few times, but haven't gotten to see the guestbook. Now I can say I have seen the most organized guild I have ever been in. After being an officer for over 22 levels I am happy to even be a part of this guild. I would rather be a regular member of a guild I like than a 3rd in command of a guild I can't enjoy because I am too busy trying to keep together. If you are in command you know what it can be like. Anyway, enough rambling. Thanks to you all for inviting me into the family.<br>
   My allegiance to Unbridled Aggresion!</TD></TR><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><TR bgcolor=#333333><TD valign=top>Posted by <B>Dammiana</B> on <B>Wednesday 10th January 2001 - 11:35:54 am</B></td><tr><td>When we last left our heroine druid, she was running away from any one of the many groups of people she has either slaughtered or avidly pissed off over the years.  Today we take another look at .. the softer side of Dammiana.  <br>
Walking up to the tree trunk where the book lay open, awaiting her signature, she ponders what to write; how to express her presence in mere words; how to let others know she had been here.  Coming to an epiphany of just what to write, she bends down to the book to find a quill and . . . .NO INK!!?!  &quot;What the hell did I come all this way for;.. to sign a book .. but there's NO INK?!  I teleported all the way from Velious to do this and nothing to show for it but my footprints??&quot;<br>
<br>
Kicking the tree trunk to express her anger, she stubs her toe and falls over, rolling down the small hillock, and smashing into ... <br>
<br>
' My what a hairy tree trunk this is.. '<br>
<br>
&quot;OH NO.. a Hill Giant!!&quot;  <br>
<br>
&quot;Ack!!  Sorry guys.  Gotta run.  See you next time... &quot;, she yells as she bolts for the zone. </TD></TR><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><TR bgcolor=#333333><TD valign=top>Posted by <B>Mike Swanner</B> on <B>Tuesday 2nd January 2001 - 12:10:14 pm</B></td><tr><td>If any one contacts Talloar, tell him I finally got into the game. I had planned on a character name of Kazshmyr but the system wouldn't take it. I'm currently doing the &quot;newbie&quot; thing at the gates of Qeynos under the name of Boeboe.</TD></TR><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><TR bgcolor=#333333><TD valign=top>Posted by <B>Tallaor</B> on <B>Tuesday 2nd January 2001 - 1:37:38 pm</B></td><tr><td>Hey man I'm glad to see you on I'll be on on Tuesday quite a bit so I might see ya then other than that my usual late nites would be the best time to find me on<br>
<br>
Cya in game<br>
Tall</TD></TR><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><TR bgcolor=#333333><TD valign=top>Posted by <B>Kazshmyr</B> on <B>Friday 29th December 2000 - 5:21:25 pm</B></td><tr><td>Greetings and salutations. In reality I'm a former coworker of Talloar. I've been trying to load into this world for 3 weeks now but am having server problems with my new PC, (it's an msn thang). The patch won't download properly. Talloar suggested that I go into this sight and introduce myself. The character I plan on running will be a human Ranger class. Aornydd' if your out there, drop me a note. I'll check the guestbook before I try to play (hopefully this weekend). I hope to see some you in Canos this weekend. Kazshmyr.</TD></TR><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><TR bgcolor=#333333><TD valign=top>Posted by <B>Sav</B> on <B>Wednesday 27th December 2000 - 9:41:05 am</B></td><tr><td>I posted here for those of you that cant get to the forums yet.You MUST send Elbrahil an e-mail to be able to post,read,etc..the other boards.His email is plastered all over the place.He will assign you a user name and password,or you can express what you would like it to be.Please try to remain ,at least,close to your game name so that we all know who you are on the boards.Welcome to all our new members and I'm lookin into our next raid,so be ready.:)One more thing,WB Elb:)</TD></TR><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><TR bgcolor=#333333><TD valign=top>Posted by <B>Scott Spencer</B> on <B>Tuesday 26th December 2000 - 12:00:07 am</B></td><tr><td>Hi all. Like to thank Savillionnow for the invite into the guild, looking forward to meeting the rest of the crew sooner or later. Arcaniss, isn't exactly a twink, but I left a few nice things to myself from an older character to get him started off on the right foot...ie: being able to buy the more useful of game tools. I don't have a lot of experience with wizards, but from watching Sav in action...I know what I wanna be when I grow up hehe. Anyway...I think at lvl 1 I am officially the youngest member...but that will change eventually. Merry Christmas to you all, and catch you in the other real world.</TD></TR><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><TR bgcolor=#333333><TD valign=top>Posted by <B>SAV</B> on <B>Monday 25th December 2000 - 12:25:29 am</B></td><tr><td>I will get all of you able to post on regular forums as soon as possible))......where did my bard buddy go or that mage fella....hehehe.....merry xmas to ya))<br>
</TD></TR><tr><td>&nbsp;</td></tr>
</TABLE>

	

